Which HTTP Status Code Matches Your DevOps Personality?


200 OK – The Calm & Reliable One
You're the "It just works" type.
 Pipelines green 
 Monitoring clean 
 Everything’s on track.
 No drama, just delivery.


301 Moved Permanently – The One Who Shifted to Cloud
“Let’s migrate this monolith to Kubernetes!”
 You’re always refactoring, modernizing, containerizing.
 Old setup? Nope.
 New infra, who dis?


403 Forbidden – The One Fighting IAM Roles
"Access Denied" is your middle name.
 You have all the YAML, but none of the permissions 😭
 Terraform apply? Error.
 kubectl get pod? Forbidden.


404 Not Found – The One on Call at 2 AM
That one alert no one understands...
 Logs? Empty.
 Dashboard? Blank.
 Infra? There.
 App? Vanished into the void.
 You're debugging what doesn't exist 😵💫


500 Internal Server Error – The One in CI/CD Chaos
You just merged to main.
 Everything broke.
 Logs are on fire.
 Manager’s pinged.
 You say:
     "It worked on dev "


429 Too Many Requests – The Overloaded One
Monitoring, logging, release, support, documentation –
 All tasks assigned to YOU.
 Mentally rate-limited.
 Still pushing through.
 Respect. 💯


502 Bad Gateway – The Blame Magnet
It’s always “network issue” until proven otherwise.
 Gateway timeout = DevOps fault.
 VPN slow = DevOps fault.
 Sun not shining? Probably DNS.




